<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Rains again delay harvest.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Rains again delay harvest.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hard red winter wheat basis bids were mostly steady on Tuesday but movement tapered off as rains in Texas and Oklahoma again slowed harvest, several cash grain dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We received some rains in Texas which we didn't want,&quot; one merchant said. &quot;That's going to delay harvest down there. It's raining in Oklahoma, too.&quot;</p>
<p>One Oklahoma dealer said he bought a small quantity of wheat on Monday which looked &quot;pretty good&quot; but he said sales were at a standstill on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Harvest was still weeks away in central Kansas.</p>
<p>&quot;You might see some wheat come off this weekend but that would be the very, very early stuff,&quot; a Kansas merchandiser said. &quot;We're still about two weeks away from where we'll see the bulk of it.&quot;</p>
